    "text": "<p>A mixture of two salts is used to prepare a solution <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>,</mo></math> which gives the following results:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>White</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>precipitate</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>only</mi><munderover><mo>&#8592;</mo><mrow><mi>Room</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>temperature</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>Dilute</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>NaOH</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></munderover><munder><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>aq</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>solution</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>of</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>the</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>salts</mi></mrow></mfenced></munder><munderover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow><mi>Room</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>temperature</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>Dilute</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>HCl</mi><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced></mrow></munderover><mi>White</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>precipitate</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>only</mi></math></p><p>The correct option&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;for the salt mixture is(are)</p>",
